#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# color_data

#% text
# `color_data(name)` is a colour scheme as a function of t in [0, 1].

#% text
# `color_data(name, t)` is its colour at t.

#% text
# `color_data(k, i)` with integers is the i-th of the plot colours.

#% text
# `color_data(name, "ColorList")` lists the scheme's colours.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A name is a gradient name (`viridis`, `thermal`, `cool_warm`, `ocean`, `earth`, `rainbow`, `gray`) or a string describing a scheme (`"rainbow"`, `"temperature"`, `"sunset"`, ...), which picks the nearest gradient.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A colour of a scheme:

#% cell
color_data("rainbow", 0.3)
#% output
#= rgb_color(0.10862745098039216, 0.6549019607843137, 0.7823529411764706)

#% text
# The scheme as a function:

#% cell
f = color_data(viridis); f(0.5)
#% output
#= rgb_color(0.13529411764705881, 0.5647058823529412, 0.5470588235294118)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The plot colours:

#% cell
table(color_data(1, i), i, 3)
#% output
#= [rgb_color(0.10588235294117647, 0.3686274509803922, 0.38823529411764707), rgb_color(0.7568627450980392, 0.3137254901960784, 0.1803921568627451), rgb_color(0.788235294117647, 0.6039215686274509, 0.1803921568627451)]

#% text
# A scheme's colours:

#% cell
color_data(ocean, "ColorList")
#% output
#= [rgb_color(0.03137254901960784, 0.11372549019607843, 0.34509803921568627), rgb_color(0.13725490196078433, 0.27450980392156865, 0.5607843137254902), rgb_color(0.1568627450980392, 0.4745098039215686, 0.7254901960784313), rgb_color(0.24705882352941178, 0.6588235294117647, 0.7686274509803922), rgb_color(0.5254901960784314, 0.8117647058823529, 0.7294117647058823), rgb_color(0.8274509803921568, 0.9333333333333333, 0.7098039215686275), rgb_color(1.0, 1.0, 0.8509803921568627)]

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# Disks coloured along a scheme:

#% cell
graphics(table([color_data("sunset", k/9), disk([k, 0], 0.45)], k, range(0, 9)))
#% output
#= image("color_data.files/color_data-5.png")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `gradient_color`, `blend`, `density_plot`
